            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0274" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/12395: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-15T20:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>142. Your 239, February 11, noon. No further action would appear to be called for
                    except to suggest to American claimants the preparation of claims covering any
                    property losses sustained as a result of acts of Japanese forces at Wuhu.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
